---
import katex from 'katex';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PostList from '../components/PostList.astro';
import PaperList from '../components/PaperList.astro';
import { getPosts, getPapers } from '../lib/content';

const kelly = katex.renderToString(String.raw`W^*(X \mid Y) - W^*(X) = I(X;Y)`, {
  displayMode: true,
});
const posts = (await getPosts()).slice(0, 5);
const papers = (await getPapers()).slice(0, 3);
---

<Base>
  <figure class="epigraph">
    <div set:html={kelly} />
    <figcaption>
      In a race with fair odds, side information <var>Y</var> raises the best achievable growth
      rate of wealth by exactly the information it carries about the outcome <var>X</var>.
      Kelly, 1956.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <section class="statement">
    <p>
      Forecasting complex systems, the ones made of billions of people deciding at once, is among
      the most important and useful things intelligence can do.
    </p>
    <p>
      I also believe it is one of the last fields free from AI. The difficult part is the framing: choosing which quantities matter,
      which assumptions survive contact with people, and which field’s tools apply. That takes
      human intuition, and I think it is where human mathematical research, aided by AI, still has
      the most to do. LLMs alone can't solve this.
    </p>
    <p>
      My work sits at the borders between information theory, game theory, physics, causality,
      reinforcement learning, and complexity science. I'm betting that these are the fields most relevant to forecasting in the age of AI.
    </p>
    <p>
      Markets are the test. Having worked in quant finance, I am convinced this is the hardest forecasting problem there is. Every idea here is set up to try to make money in the financial system.
    </p>
    <p>This site is where I write up what I learn and publish papers as they’re finished.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2><a href="/writing/">Writing</a></h2>
    <PostList posts={posts} />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2><a href="/papers/">Papers</a></h2>
    <PaperList papers={papers} />
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .epigraph {
    margin: 0 0 3.5rem;
  }
  .epigraph :global(.katex-display) {
    margin: 0;
    text-align: left;
  }
  .epigraph :global(.katex-display > .katex) {
    text-align: left;
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 5.8vw, 1.85rem);
  }
  .epigraph figcaption {
    max-width: 30rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }
  .epigraph var {
    font-style: italic;
  }
  .statement p:first-child {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  h2 a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  h2 a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--rule);
  }
</style>
